## Monokulo onion service. Add to /etc/tor/torrc (or a file it %includes),
## adjust the directory, then reload tor. Every line is explained in
## docs/TOR.md. Needs tor >= 0.4.8 built with the proof-of-work module:
## `tor --list-modules` must print `pow: yes`.
##
## Monokulo side: set the admin setting `abuse.onion_listener` (or
## MONOKULO_ABUSE_ONION_LISTENER) to 127.0.0.1:8082 and restart monokulo.
## `public_url` should be this service's http://<address>.onion (see
## <HiddenServiceDir>/hostname once tor has started).

HiddenServiceDir /var/lib/tor/monokulo/
HiddenServiceVersion 3
# Port 80 of the .onion goes to monokulo's loopback onion listener, which
# requires the PROXY header below. Never point it at monokulo's ordinary
# port (127.0.0.1:8081): that one ignores PROXY headers, so every visitor
# would look like the same client, 127.0.0.1.
HiddenServicePort 80 127.0.0.1:8082

# Tell monokulo which Tor circuit each connection arrived on (a PROXY v1
# header with the circuit id in an fc00::/16 source address). One circuit
# is one visitor, so monokulo can limit and challenge circuits separately.
HiddenServiceExportCircuitID haproxy

# Proof-of-work at the introduction step: under load, tor asks clients to
# solve a puzzle whose effort rises with the attack. Tor Browser does this
# automatically, no JavaScript involved.
HiddenServicePoWDefensesEnabled 1
# How many rendezvous requests a second tor hands on from the PoW queue,
# and the burst it allows.
HiddenServicePoWQueueRate 50
HiddenServicePoWQueueBurst 250

# Rate-limit introductions at the introduction points themselves, before
# they reach this machine.
HiddenServiceEnableIntroDoSDefense 1
HiddenServiceEnableIntroDoSRatePerSec 25
HiddenServiceEnableIntroDoSBurstPerSec 200

# At most 64 simultaneous streams (connections) per circuit, and close the
# circuit of anyone who tries for more. A normal visitor needs a handful
# of page and API connections plus at most 16 live-update streams per
# store (monokulo's own cap), so 64 leaves plenty of room.
HiddenServiceMaxStreams 64
HiddenServiceMaxStreamsCloseCircuit 1
